# ====== Java / Spring Boot ======
**/target/
*.jar
*.war
*.class
*.log

# ====== Node / React ======
**/node_modules/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
# .env at repo root — this is the actual secrets file (JWT_SECRET, DB/RabbitMQ
# passwords) created via `cp .env.example .env`. The original pattern here was
# `_env` (a typo — matches a literal filename "_env", not dotfiles) plus
# `*/.env`, which only matches .env inside a subdirectory. Neither pattern
# covers the root .env, so it was never actually gitignored — a real risk of
# committing live secrets. Both now fixed below.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
.env.*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ====== Misc ======
**.zip
.github/
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example

# ====== IDE / Editors ======
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.project
*.classpath
*.settings/

# Backstage build outputs
**/dist/
**/dist-types/
**/build/
**/packages/*/dist/
**/plugins/*/dist/
**/coverage/

# TypeScript / build caches
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.cache/
.tmp/

# Test artifacts
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# Yarn 4 generated/cache files that should not be committed
**/.yarn/install-state.gz
**/.yarn/build-state.yml
**/.yarn/unplugged/
**/.yarn/cache/

# Local Backstage configuration / secrets
app-config.local.yaml
app-config.*.local.yaml